Package: balancing
Title: Optimization-Based Balancing Weights for Causal Inference
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Malcolm", "Barrett", , "malcolmbarrett@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0299-5825")),
    person("The authors of the vendored Rust crates", role = "cph",
           comment = "see src/rust/Cargo.lock and the bundled crate sources for the full list")
  )
Description: Calculates optimization-based balancing weights for causal
    inference, including entropy balancing, inverse probability tilting,
    the covariate balancing propensity score, energy balancing,
    characteristic function distance balancing, and stable balancing
    weights. Weights target covariate balance directly by solving a convex
    optimization problem, with support for binary, categorical, and
    continuous exposures across a range of causal estimands. A Rust core
    provides the numerical solvers.
